    "definition": "Problem266 fixes preorder variables and defines dec(k) inclusively. Hence d(F) is nonempty for n≥1, contains no empty set, and includes each variable at least once. The same problem counts both terminals when it gives n+2 nodes for a(F).",
    "printedChineseAndEnglish": {
      "leaf": "ζ(T)=1 if |T|=1",
      "tree": "ζ(T)=1+Σζ(T_i)+|T|−|T_k| for last child T_k",
      "forest": "Z(d(F))=1+Σζ(T_i)+[|T_k|=1] for last tree T_k",
      "minimum": "n, attained by a forest of n singleton trees",
      "maximum": "floor(n²/4)+2n+1; for odd n=2m−1 take node k with children k+1 and k+m for 1≤k<m",
      "treeFunctionalEquation": "Z(w,z)=wz+w²zZ(w,z)/(1−Z(w,wz))",
      "printedIntermediateDerivative": "Z_w(1,z)=z/s+z/s²; s=sqrt(1−4z)",
      "forestGeneratingFunction": "(wZ(w,z)+w³z−w²z)/(1−Z(w,z))",
      "printedForestDerivative": "z/(1−4z)+2z/s",
      "printedMean": "(4^(n−1)+2n C_(n−1))/C_n"
    },
    "independentReasoning": {
      "minimum": {
        "replacement": "n+2",
        "proof": [
          "Every variable occurs in some member, requiring at least one internal node labeled by that variable in its ZDD. A nonempty family reaches top, and because the empty set is absent, following only low arcs leads to bottom.",
          "The forest of n singleton trees has a chain of n nodes with high arcs to top and last low arc to bottom. Thus it achieves n+2. For n=1 the graph (1,bottom,top) has 3 nodes, agreeing with the printed forest size recurrence and printed mean."
        ]
      },
      "maximum": {
        "replacement": "n+1+floor(n²/4) for n≥2; 3 for n=1",
        "counterexample": [
          "For n=3 the very tree named as extremizer in the source is a root with two leaves. Its ζ=1+1+1+3−1=5, so Z=6, whereas the purported maximum is 9.",
          "Its descendant family is {{1,2,3},{2},{3}} with four internal ZDD nodes (two distinct nodes labeled 2, one each labeled 1 and 3) and both terminals."
        ],
        "proofFromPrintedRecurrence": [
          "Put S(T)=ζ(T)−|T| and g(n)=floor(n²/4). The first differences of g are nondecreasing and g(0)=0, so g is superadditive on nonnegative integers.",
          "For nonleaf T of size n, let a≥1 be the size of its last child, and b=n−1−a the total size of its earlier children. Then S(T)=Σ S(T_i)+b+1≤g(a)+g(b)+b+1 by induction and superadditivity. The latter expression, as an integer function of a with a+b fixed, is discretely convex. Its endpoint values for a=1 and a=n−1 are g(n−2)+n−1=g(n) and g(n−1)+1≤g(n).",
          "Equality is realized by a single leaf when n=1 and by a root with a last child of size one and an earlier recursively extremizing child of size n−2 when that size is positive. For n=2 the sole child is a leaf. The construction is nonleaf when n≥2, and for odd n≥3 is the ordered comb specified in the source.",
          "For any forest whose last tree is nonleaf, the extra sum is at most g(n), by superadditivity, and the indicator is 0. If the last tree is a leaf then its S=0 and the extra sum is at most g(n−1); the indicator contributes 1, so Z≤n+g(n−1)+2≤n+g(n)+1 for n≥2. A forest consisting of just the nonleaf extremizer achieves the bound. For n=1 separately evaluate the original recurrence to get 3."
        ]
      },
      "intermediateDerivative": {
        "replacement": "z/s+z/(4s²)−z/4",
        "proof": [
          "Let T=Z(1,z)=(1−s)/2, D=1−T and U=Z_w(1,z). Use z=TD and Z_z(1,z)=1/s. The derivative in w of Z(w,wz) at 1 is U+z/s, which must be included.",
          "Differentiating the full printed functional equation gives U=z+2zT/D+zU/D+zT(U+z/s)/D². The coefficient on U brought to the left is s/D. Solving gives U=z(1+T)/s+T²z/s²=z/s+z/(4s²)−z/4.",
          "The one vertex tree gives coefficient [z]U=1 and the one ordered tree with two vertices gives [z²]U=3. The printed intermediate line instead gives 2 and 6."
        ]
      },
      "meanFormula": {
        "disposition": "retain original exact derivative and final mean",
        "proof": "Differentiating the printed forest generating function using the corrected U gives T/D+z/D+U/D²=z/s²+2z/s. Coefficient extraction and division by C_n therefore still give the original exact mean."
      }
    },
